64,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,678,6351,5109,400,89,3,1741,429,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,19,15170,89,481,220,23,92,1124,1291,91,14581,220,16,11,90155,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,16,17,15170,89,481,220,23,72,92,1124,1291,91,14581,1124,37018,90,20,15170,18,27275,59,408,90,6612,9,92,6269,678,279,9904,11,18663,553,76602,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind all complex numbers $z$ such that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| &= 1, \\\\\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| &= \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\end{align*}Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5618e45fbb00d0bfe32a1ab22abc3548de9cb2e55a52ab701bfcaafcf1d1ea4c"},"seconds":57.406503438949585,"seed":1126450198636393943,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for all complex numbers \\( z \\) that satisfy the given conditions, we start with the first equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| = 1\n\\]\n\nThis equation implies that the distance from \\( z \\) to 4 is equal to the distance from \\( z \\) to 8. Hence, \\( z \\) lies on the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining the points 4 and 8. The midpoint of this segment is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4 + 8}{2} = 6\n\\]\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of the segment joining 4 and 8 is a vertical line through \\( x = 6 \\). Therefore, \\( z \\) must have the form \\( z = 6 + bi \\) for some real number \\( b \\).\n\nNext, we use the second equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( z = 6 + bi \\) into this equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{(6 + bi) - 12}{(6 + bi) - 8i} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{-6 + bi}{6 + (b-8)i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the magnitudes of the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\left| -6 + bi \\right| = \\sqrt{36 + b^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\left| 6 + (b-8)i \\right| = \\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{36 + b^2}}{\\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}} = \\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nSquaring both sides, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{36 + b^2}{36 + (b-8)^2} = \\frac{25}{9}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\n\\[\n9(36 + b^2) = 25(36 + (b-8)^2)\n\\]\n\nExpanding both sides:\n\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25(b^2 - 16b + 64)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25b^2 - 400b + 1600\n\\]\n\nSimplifying:\n\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 2500 + 25b^2 - 400b\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms:\n\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 - 2500 - 25b^2 + 400b = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-16b^2 + 400b - 2176 = 0\n\\]\n\nDividing the entire equation by -16:\n\n\\[\nb^2 - 25b + 136 = 0\n\\]\n\nUsing the quadratic formula \\( b = \\frac{-B \\pm \\sqrt{B^2 - 4AC}}{2A} \\):\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{25 \\pm \\sqrt{625 - 544}}{2} = \\frac{25 \\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} = \\frac{25 \\pm 9}{2}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( b \\):\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{34}{2} = 17 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = \\frac{16}{2} = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the solutions for \\( z \\) are:\n\n\\[\nz = 6 + 17i \\quad \\text{and} \\quad z = 6 + 8i\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the solutions are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 8i, 6 + 17i}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6 + 8i, 6 + 17i}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
